{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787175152124833001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"dandruffy-insolent-goosefish","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ed87a49ed282c2c3554ed433ae7af1ded14561c5af75b566c25764436f2721f3","event_uuid":"b7455b2d-e4fa-43c4-9a12-3def33a80630","position":{"commit_sha":"0c515f8680a3a6988947a1ec18680b5b7ca9b07d","position":"1787172515610120001-b7455b2d-e4fa-43c4-9a12-3def33a80630"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"78b16b9c6c746251baa91d8638973b9bd4a16316f530442e778bf39f8d203df7","event_uuid":"1c5f19d6-d37e-4241-93b9-9079688cfc50","position":{"commit_sha":"43c727bc90d40b9caf95cc1d3cbae6e30d3d7dc3","position":"1787172542824450001-1c5f19d6-d37e-4241-93b9-9079688cfc50"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787172515610120001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1c5f19d6-d37e-4241-93b9-9079688cfc50","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d30c-f491-395f-432e"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`AcliClient.search_issues` (`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py:413-453`)\nmemoizes its full result set per JQL string in `self._search_cache` — an unbounded dict with **no\nTTL and no invalidation anywhere in the class** — and it caches **negative (empty) answers** too:\n\n    if jql not in self._search_cache:      # acli.py:417\n        ... run the acli subprocess ...\n        self._search_cache[jql] = all_issues    # acli.py:451\n    all_issues = self._search_cache[jql]        # acli.py:453\n\nThe docstring (acli.py:409) scopes the cache to \"avoid redundant fetches when the caller\npaginates\", but nothing enforces that scope. Any caller that re-asks the same JQL over time on a\nclient that outlives one pagination sequence receives a permanently stale answer.\n\nThis is not hypothetical: it is the proven root cause of bug d30c (dutiable-shaded-honeyeater),\nwhere an index-visibility poll re-issued two constant JQLs on one client and only the first\nattempt ever reached Jira.\n\n## Why this is a latent trap, not just a d30c detail\n\nThe only correct handling in the tree reaches into a **private attribute** from outside the class:\n`access_check.py:152-158` does `cache.pop(jql, None)` before each retry. d30c's fix does the same\nat the E2E poll site. So the invariant \"a caller that needs freshness must evict `_search_cache`\nitself\" is (a) undocumented, (b) unenforced, and (c) satisfied by two independent call sites\nreaching through the client's encapsulation.\n\nCallers worth auditing:\n\n- `binding_recovery.py:342-346` — searches `labels = \"rebar-id:<local_id>\"` and accumulates\n  `search_miss_count` **across passes**, with the explicit comment that \"A NEGATIVE SEARCH IS NOT\n  PROOF OF ABSENCE ON DC (bug 21fc)\" and that absence must be corroborated by *repeated* misses.\n  That corroboration is only meaningful if each pass issues a genuinely fresh query. If the\n  `AcliClient` built at `runtime.py:145` / `adapters/jira/backend.py:359` persists across passes,\n  repeated misses would be N replays of one cached answer — and `_MISSES_BEFORE_UNBIND` could\n  unbind a binding whose issue exists, causing the duplicate-create that bug 21fc was written to\n  prevent. **Client lifetime across passes was not established during the d30c investigation and\n  is the first thing to check.**\n- `dispatch_one.py:149`, `fetch_paging.py:86` — believed safe (single query / genuine pagination),\n  but should be confirmed by the audit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Establish whether an `AcliClient` instance can span more than one reconcile pass, and\n  document the answer where the cache is defined.\n- [ ] Give the cache a supported freshness door instead of private-attribute reach-in — e.g. a\n  `search_issues(..., fresh=True)` kwarg or an `invalidate_search_cache(jql=None)` method — and\n  migrate `access_check.py` and the d30c E2E poll onto it.\n- [ ] Document at `acli.py:409` that negative results are cached and that repeat-query callers\n  must bypass the memo.\n- [ ] Audit `binding_recovery.py:342-346` specifically and either prove it is unaffected or fix it\n  with a test that fails without the fix.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3288-aa58-54d0-4c19","ticket_type":"task","title":"Give AcliClient's per-JQL search memo a supported freshness door (it caches negatives forever)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b7455b2d-e4fa-43c4-9a12-3def33a80630","1c5f19d6-d37e-4241-93b9-9079688cfc50"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787175152124833001,"uuid":"080b657b-22ec-4fc1-9f87-7cddab7515b0"}